\documentclass{article}
\title{Pipelined Consensus for High-Throughput Blockchains}
\author{Anon}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\begin{abstract}
Blockchains are popular. Consensus is the bottleneck. Many protocols exist. We built a simulator. Our protocol pipelines the voting phase. Throughput is important. We ran experiments with 128 nodes. Latency matters for users. The results show 2.4x throughput improvement. We compared with two baselines. Confirmation latency drops by 35 percent. The protocol is safe under partial synchrony. Future work will study sharding.
\end{abstract}
\section{Introduction}
Consensus protocols order transactions in distributed ledgers.
\end{document}
